<messaging:emailTemplate subject=" {!relatedTo.NSP_AIMS_Client_Name__c} ({!relatedTo.NSP_AIMS_ClientNo__c}) / XML Time Import Request " recipientType="User" relatedToType="Implementation_Profile__c">
<messaging:HtmlEmailBody >
<html>
  <body>
  <table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5">
  <c:InsperityEmailHeader ></c:InsperityEmailHeader>
  <p> <span style="color:red">ATTACH THE XML OPTIONS DOCUMENT AND FORWARD THE EMAIL BELOW TO YOUR CLIENT TO GATHER NEEDED INFORMATION FOR XML TIME IMPORT. </span>  </p> 
  <p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- </p>
  
  <p>Dear Client:</p>
  <p>When considering using a third party application to upload payroll, any system can be used if the system 
  can export a properly formatted file using one of two options.  I have attached a document that also
   outlines the 2 different approaches mentioned below.</p>
   
<p>The only type of file that can be uploaded through Insperity Premier is an Insperity formatted xml
 file.  We have two approaches that clients can use to generate the XML file.  The preferred method is for
 the client to work with their vendor to create a direct export out of their time system using the Insperity
 XML schema and sample files.   Similar to how it is done with Insperity time and attendance.  This is the
 most straight forward method for the client as it does not involve multiple steps.  Our team can provide
support by testing any payroll files generated by the vendor to ensure the meet the schema requirements.</p>

<p>The other approach if the client cannot export an XML file is to use our conversion utility.  This utility is
 used to convert a .CSV or .TXT file into a properly formatted XML file for upload.  The utility does add an
 additional step to the process as the file must be converted before it can be uploaded for payroll.  We
 typically send out the attached document to explain the two different methods.  Once the client decides
 which method may work best for them we can send out the proper file specifications.</p>
 
<p>Just an FYI if the client decides to use our utility there is development time involved with getting it
 configured for the client and the client would need to be running Windows PC’s, the utility will not work
 on Macs.  Also this would be for the purpose of submitting payroll, this does not include any type of
 interface to send data back to an accounting or general ledger system. </p>

  
  
  
<p>Regards,<br/>
{!relatedTo.NSP_Project_Manager__r.Name}<br/>
{!relatedTo.NSP_Project_Manager__r.NSP_Job_Title__c}</p>
<c:InsperityEmailFooter ></c:InsperityEmailFooter>

</table> 
</body>
</html>
</messaging:HtmlEmailBody>
  
</messaging:emailTemplate>